<title>AUSTRALIA: Foster's sees top 5 ranking in U.S.</title>
<headline>Foster's sees top 5 ranking in U.S.</headline>
<dateline>MELBOURNE 1997-02-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>Foster's might rank among the top five U.S. beer brands in calendar 1997, Foster's Brewing Group chief executive Ted Kunkel said on Monday.</p>
<p>&quot;In the U.S., further expansion of sales of Foster's will be a priority. We could well push up to be in the top five (beer) brands in the U.S. this year,&quot; Kunkel told a news conference.  </p>
<p>He said Foster's international unit, which controls the Foster's brand outside Australia, aimed to increased its licensing presence in South America over 1997.</p>
<p>Foster's earlier announced a 2.4 percent increase in net earnings to A$169.4 million for the six months to December 31.</p>
<p>-- Melbourne bureau 61-3 9286-1435</p>
